From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ari Chivukula <arichiv@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:36:35 -0700
Subject: [Clear-Site-Data] Prevent cross-site fetch clearing unpartitioned
 data

Currently, cross-site fetch requests with CSD headers clear
unpartitioned storage. This is incorrect, as they should only clear the
relevant partitioned storage. This CL ensures the StorageKey used for
CSD logic is set up properly with trusted data from the network service.

Fixed: 566660676, 518053309, 550356947
Change-Id: I4b7e845a92d4ea09ff08da3342c57ec7d50d0f69
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8463605
Reviewed-by: mmenke <mmenke@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Ari Chivukula <arichiv@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Charlie Reis <creis@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Ari Chivukula <arichiv@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Lambros Lambrou <lambroslambrou@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Erik Chen <erikchen@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1709414}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
Context adaptations only: the mojom already imported unguessable_token.mojom and shared_storage.mojom on this branch (duplicate import dropped), StoragePartitionImpl::URLLoaderNetworkContext keeps this branch's shape (no DeviceBoundSessionContext), and OnClearSiteData() keeps its DCHECK(initialized_) ahead of the new cookie-partition-key consistency checks. The new top_level_site/nonce plumbing, CalculateStorageKeyForClearSiteData() and the network-service side applied unchanged. Electron's own network::mojom::URLLoaderNetworkServiceObserver implementation (shell/browser/net/url_loader_network_observer) is updated for the new OnClearSiteData() signature in a separate Electron commit.

